    "title":"Combined method citations",
    "description":"Water measurement methods joined with their method category, their method citations and those citations' descriptions \u2014 the same content as the `methods`, `method-categories`, `method-citations` and `citations` collections, denormalized so one request describes a method fully. A method with several citations appears once per citation, all sharing the same `method_id`; a method with no citation appears once with the citation fields null. The `id` is synthetic (`&lt;method_id&gt;.&lt;citation_method_id&gt;`, with `0` standing in for \"no citation\") because no single source column identifies a row. This collection is non-spatial: method records carry no geometry, so bbox/spatial filters are not supported.\n",
